WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.830
In addition to welcoming back most of the
familiar faces of the series, the new season

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.730
of Stranger Things will introduce a few newcomers,
from an intriguing lifeguard to an ambitious

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:10.240
politician.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.360
But even if they're new to Hawkins, some of
these actors just might look familiar.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:20.180
There's no doubt that Cary Elwes' credentials
precede his arrival as Mayor Larry Kline in

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.200
Stranger Things 3.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.420
But what's hard to pinpoint is exactly which
role he's most famous for.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:30.060
Fantasy fans probably know him best as the
romantic swordsman Westley in The Princess

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.160
Bride or perhaps the title role in Robin Hood:
Men in Tights.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.700
For horror fans, though, it's more likely
that his turns as Lord Arthur Holmwood in

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.860
Bram Stoker's Dracula or Dr. Lawrence Gordon
in Saw left the biggest marks.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:47.180
Meanwhile, others might remember Elwes more
as antagonist Russ Wheeler in Days of Thunder

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.450
or as a cocky tornado scientist in Twister.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.600
He may even be familiar to TV fans for his
appearances in series like The X-Files or

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.360
Psych, to name a few.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.540
No matter what he's best known for, he definitely
comes into Stranger Things as the most veteran

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:01.700
newcomer of the bunch.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:07.380
Things are just heating up for Maya Hawke's
career as she joins Stranger Things as the

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.340
ice cream-slinging Robin, but she's been a
part of show business her entire life.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.360
She's the oldest child of Ethan Hawke and
Uma Thurman, and was born shortly after her

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.820
folks met on the set of 1997's Gattaca.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:23.980
She was raised away from the limelight, but
even at a young age she still dove right into

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.680
local theatrical productions and is now following
in her parents' footsteps by pursuing an acting

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.200
career.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.200
Hawke made her onscreen debut in the PBS miniseries
adaptation of Little Women as Jo March, who

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.340
refuses to conform to the gender expectations
of her era.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.540
Soon after, she appeared in the indie thriller
Ladyworld.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.880
Her post-Stranger Things resume is already
set to make her even more recognizable.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:51.420
The buzziest of her upcoming projects is probably
Quentin Tarantino's Once Upon a Time in Hollywood.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.560
Like Maya Hawke, Jake Busey is an heir to
a Hollywood legacy who bears a striking resemblance

00:01:57.580 --> 00:01:58.400
to his famous parent.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.380
He's the son of the inimitable Gary Busey
and has the same white-blonde hair and toothy

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.200
grin as his father.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:09.170
In addition to their similar appearances,
a look at his filmography reveals that Busey

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:13.420
also seems to share his dad's penchant for
action-oriented movies and TV shows.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.871
The younger Busey's career began in 1978,
when he appeared alongside his father in the

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.740
film Straight Time.

00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:24.380
His credits really started to build up in
the '90s in the likes of Contact and Starship

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:24.880
Troopers.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:29.530
More recently, he showed up in 2018's The
Predator and has guest starred on shows like

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.760
Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.340
Ultimately, it was his turn as a psychotic
serial killer in 1996's The Frighteners that

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.900
got the attention of the Duffer Brothers and
inspired them to write the role of Bruce,

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.220
a newspaper journalist with loose morals and
a sick sense of humor.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.239
"Oh, Patricia.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.620
You kill her.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.420
I'll watch."

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:56.200
Before becoming new lifeguard Heather in Stranger
Things 3, Francesca Reale had already made

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.460
a name for herself on another Netflix original.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.610
In the sitcom Haters Back Off!, she starred
as Emily, the very normal sister of the very

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.240
abnormal Miranda Sings.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.320
“What is a bag of salami?"

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.380
"Emily, you know what a bag of salami is."

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:11.940
"Don't play dumb.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.200
We all know what a bag of salami is."

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.580
Apart from that series and a guest spot in
a 2016 episode of Blue Bloods, Reale's still

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.200
very much an actress who's in the midst of
breaking through.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:26.019
Like many up-and-comers, she's been steadily
establishing a reel with appearances in short

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:30.160
films with names like "The Furies of War,"
"Goodbye Charm City," and "Cabin."

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.500
She could also be seen sharing the screen
with Stranger Things co-star Natalia Dyer

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.500
in the 2019 teen drama Yes, God, Yes.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.940
She might be new to the biz, but Caroline
Arapoglou is quickly rising through the ranks

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:46.540
of TV stars ahead of her appearance as Winnie
in Stranger Things 3.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:51.810
She got her start with bit roles on shows
like Atlanta and films like Hot Summer Nights.

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.580
She later nabbed a recurring role as lab tech
Noni Turner on The Resident.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.620
Arapoglou also appeared in one episode of
The Walking Dead's ninth season as zombie

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.000
apocalypse survivor Rose.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.819
After Stranger Things, she'll continue to
work on Netflix on the drama series Outer

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:10.280
Banks, and she's also busy cultivating her
career in live theater.

